% test_no_readers.glp - the no_readers/1 guard: succeeds on writers, suspends on readers
%
% Replaces the loose programs/tests/test_no_readers.glp, which posted its three
% cases with the `?-` directive form the parser has no handling for, so it
% loaded by no route and its cases ran nowhere.  All three were ground terms.
% The property that separates no_readers from ground — a term carrying a writer
% and no reader succeeds — went untested, as did suspension.

exported procedure test_no_readers(_?, Constant).
test_no_readers(X, ok) :- no_readers(X?) | true.
